{"availability":"available","full":"benconnor1972/BODAQS","name":"BODAQS","description":"Bicycle Open Data Acquisition System","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":8,"forks":1,"created":"2025-11-06T11:02:28Z","updated":"2026-10-11T07:10:30Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://demo.bodaqs.net/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:55.220Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:55.220Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:55.220Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T07:26:55.220Z","stars":8,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["BODAQS (Bicycle open data acquisition system) is an open-source, build-it-yourself data collection and analysis system for mountain bikes, designed to be accessible to anyone with some DIY skills and a curiosity about what their bike is actually doing.","Data acquisition is ubiquitous in motorsport, and it's making its way into mountain-bike racing too. But for the engineering-minded (or budget-constrained), the choice is often between costly professional systems or consumer tools that keep the underlying data hidden.","BODAQS aims to offer an alternative: hardware that can be built with basic soldering skills using widely available parts; software with deep functionality and a structure designed for long-term expansion; and analysis built on powerful, free tools — alongside mounting and mechanical designs that can be 3D printed at home or produced at low cost."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/benconnor1972/BODAQS/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"7b0186946ae00cd3065b9a3ee76ea423122d3bb42dd68a9ff027c238dd024727","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:55.302Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:55.302Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"BODAQS (Bicycle open data acquisition system) is an open-source, build-it-yourself data collection and analysis system for mountain bikes, designed to be ac